schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-EXPORT
wu: E-EXPORT.W1
branch: wu/export/paging
tests:
  unit:
    count: 14
    covers: "src/store.rs Store::page - the walk is newest-first and terminates without a cursor across three pages; a page that exactly empties the ring reports next_cursor null (the peek-one-past behaviour, so a caller stops on the cursor and never on an empty page); a limit beyond the ring returns everything once; an empty ring is empty and final; paging walks the filtered set not the whole ring; a cursor the ring no longer holds ends the walk instead of restarting at the newest row; a cursor the filter excludes still positions the walk (the cursor is a ring position, resolved before filtering); an insert between pages stays behind the walk. Two proptests: paging_a_live_ring_never_duplicates_or_skips drives inserts between pages over arbitrary seed/churn/limit/cap and asserts no id served twice, the walk terminates within budget, and every row present at the start and still held was reached - the WU's central claim, proven as a property; a_page_walk_matches_the_unpaged_listing_on_a_still_ring asserts paging re-slices list() rather than redefining it. src/api/routes.rs list_flows - no limit yields the bare array, a limit yields the envelope and its cursor follow-up ends with next_cursor null, paging composes with host filtering, and five refusals (limit=0, limit=none, limit=-1, a non-uuid cursor, a cursor with no limit) each 400 naming the parameter."
  integration:
    count: 4
    covers: "tests/api.rs over the real axum router. the_unparameterised_listing_keeps_its_pre_paging_shape locks the summary row's field set on a paging-free GET /flows, so a field joining or leaving the row is a red test rather than a silent wire change. walking_by_cursor_yields_exactly_the_unpaged_listing walks ?limit=2 by cursor to exhaustion and asserts the id sequence equals the single unpaged read, unfiltered and under host=keep, with every page bounded by its limit - paging is a re-slicing of the listing, never a second implementation. the_router_refuses_malformed_paging_by_name asserts each 400 body names the offending parameter. a_cursor_the_ring_evicted_ends_the_walk_rather_than_restarting_it drives a real byte-cap eviction and asserts the empty, final page."
  e2e:
    waived: "The epic's own e2e (tests/e2e_export.rs, step 2 of the epic plan's e2e table: GET /flows?limit=1 then follow the cursor to the end, asserting every captured flow seen exactly once) covers W1 end-to-end over real proxied traffic and lands with the epic. Nothing about a query parameter is provable at e2e level that the epic's step does not prove, and a second engine boot for it is duplicated cost rather than coverage. The regression evidence that this WU left the unparameterised listing alone is that both existing e2e suites (e2e_capture, e2e_h2), which read GET /flows without paging parameters, run green unchanged and no existing test was touched."
note: "E-EXPORT.W1 delivers opt-in paging on GET /flows over Store::page - one reversed walk of the ring under one lock, resumed by consuming the walk up to and including the cursor id. The cursor names a row rather than an offset, which is what makes the walk safe against a live capture: a concurrent insert lands newer than the cursor and so sits behind the walk, an eviction only removes rows the walk would have reached, and an evicted cursor row ends the walk honestly rather than restarting at the newest row and re-serving everything the caller holds. The wire contract stays additive - no limit means the bare array every existing client already reads, limit means an envelope because an array cannot carry a cursor - so src/api/ui.html, ui/src/ and every pre-existing test are outside this diff. limit deserializes as a String so a non-numeric value becomes our own 400 naming the parameter instead of axum's anonymous query rejection. No UI-rendering file in the diff. cargo test green (79 lib, 15 api, 3 ca, 6 e2e_capture, 4 e2e_h2); clippy pedantic clean with --all-targets; fmt clean."
